  "narrative": "For all delivered discovery estimates, I use the signed-estimate convention: for direction -1 main effects, positive means stronger dependency; for direction +1 main effects, positive means weaker dependency; for interactions, positive means the signed main effect is larger in the focal subgroup than in its complement. Because dependency scores are negative, I judge the 10 percent clinical threshold approximately against absolute mean-scale scores and also against outcome SD. H123 MSI-high versus WRN within adherent cultures showed +0.813 [0.780,0.846], H60 MSI-high versus WRN within batch_a showed +0.824 [0.766,0.882], H124 PTEN loss versus STAT3 within adherent cultures showed +0.262 [0.203,0.321], and H58 PTEN loss versus STAT3 within batch_a showed +0.234 [0.125,0.342]. These are all large relative to their outcome scales and intervals exclude clinically relevant nulls, so I accept them as robust dataset-specific context confirmations. H125 and H126 directly stratified PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency by EMT state: EMT-high +0.353 [0.244,0.463] and EMT lower-or-equal +0.236 [0.177,0.295]. Both are meaningful and precise, but the difference between them is not an established interaction because the H116 interaction interval crossed zero. I close the H116 EMT-interaction investigation as unresolved rather than accepting modification. H127 STK11 and H128 SMAD4 STAT3 effects were small and imprecise, with point differences under the approximate 10 percent threshold, so reject. H129 PIK3CA versus EGFR bypass was opposite and null; H130 NF1 versus EGFR bypass was tiny; reject. H132 BRCA2 versus KIF18A was opposite and null; reject. H131 PTEN loss within KRAS-mutant lines gave the only candidate new effect: +0.0639 [0.0196,0.1082] in the registered weaker-KRAS-dependency direction, about 0.36 SD. The point estimate is plausible and exceeds 10 percent against the overall absolute KRAS mean, but the lower bound is roughly 8 percent and the claim has not been independently validated. Given multiplicity and possible co-mutational confounding, I keep H131 unresolved and request independent validation rather than accepting immediately. H114 is closed unresolved because the adherent PTEN-STAT3 main effect is robust but the culture interaction remains unsupported or uncertain.",
  "research_notes": "Round-10 appraise. Signed convention: direction -1 positive means stronger dependency; direction +1 positive means weaker dependency; positive interaction means larger signed main effect in focal subgroup. Current accepted core context confirmations include MSI-high WRN overall, TP53-loss subset, Avana, batch_a, and adherent direct; KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency; SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency; PTEN-loss stronger STAT3 dependency overall, PIK3CA subset, TP53-wt, adherent direct, batch_a, and both EMT-high and EMT lower-or-equal strata. H131 PTEN-loss within KRAS-mutant lines for weaker KRAS dependency is pending validation: point moderate but lower bound below 10 percent; validation requested. If independent validation is positive and interval supports meaningful magnitude, accept; if null or conflicting, reject or close. Negative new predictors: STK11 and SMAD4 for STAT3; PIK3CA and NF1 for EGFR weaker-dependency bypass; BRCA2 for KIF18A stronger dependency. EMT interaction H116 closed unresolved: PTEN-STAT3 effect present in both EMT strata, difference not established. Adherent culture interaction H114 closed unresolved: main effect robust, interaction unsupported or uncertain. Multiplicity caution remains. Validation requests remaining after this request: 2. Future analyses should focus mainly on H131 validation result or new effects that are large, precise, directionally consistent, and relevant to accepted mechanisms.",
