  "narrative": "I use the signed convention throughout: for direction -1 main effects, positive signed values mean stronger dependency; for direction +1 main effects, positive signed values mean weaker dependency; for interactions, positive signed values mean the signed main effect is larger in the focal subgroup than in its complement. For the approximately 10% clinically meaningful benchmark, I compare estimates against the absolute mean dependency scale for the relevant outcome, with additional attention to precision and multiplicity. H133 tested whether AXL-high expression amplifies the PTEN-loss STAT3 association: signed interaction +0.037 [-0.083,0.157]. The point estimate is modest relative to the core PTEN-STAT3 effect and the interval is wide and compatible with clinically important effects in either direction, so this does not support a meaningful AXL-context modification. H134 tested stemness-high context: signed interaction -0.019 [-0.133,0.094], null and imprecise, so also rejected. H135 tested whether SLFN11 expression modifies MSI-high WRN dependency: signed interaction +0.057 [-0.002,0.116]. This is the only newly delivered borderline candidate. The point estimate is above the approximate 10% absolute-scale threshold for WRN, and biologically SLFN11 could interact with MSI/damage-response biology, but the 95% interval just includes zero and this is one of many context-interaction tests. Therefore I do not accept it from discovery evidence alone; I keep H135 unresolved and active and request independent validation because it is the most plausible remaining new context effect. The MYC-amplification STAT3 hypotheses are not supported. H136 gave -0.004 [-0.034,0.026]; H139 gave -0.008 [-0.050,0.034] in MYC-RNA-high lines; H140 gave +0.007 [-0.042,0.056] in MYC-RNA-low lines. All are small and imprecise, with no evidence for a stronger STAT3 dependency in MYC-amplified lines or an expression-dependent restriction. CDKN2A loss for SMARCA2 dependency independent of SMARCA4 loss, H137, gave +0.002 [-0.022,0.026], near-null; rejected. H138 tested PTEN loss as a weaker-EGFR-dependency bypass predictor and gave -0.006 [-0.029,0.017] in the weaker-dependency direction, opposite but tiny; rejected. H141 tested TP53 loss for weaker MDM2 dependency within MYC-amplified lines and gave only +0.012 [-0.058,0.081], too small and imprecise to support the mechanistic hypothesis. The specificity probes support the selectivity of accepted core associations: H144 MSI-high with KIF18A was -0.003 [-0.039,0.033], rejecting extension of the MSI effect beyond WRN; H145 PTEN loss with POLR2A was +0.004 [-0.019,0.028], and H146 PTEN loss with DHX9 was -0.002 [-0.026,0.021], both null, supporting STAT3 specificity rather than a broad PTEN-loss transcription/replication effect. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
