  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted using the already-signed convention. For direction -1, a positive estimate means stronger dependency, i.e. a more negative dependency score; for direction +1, a positive estimate means weaker dependency. The approximately 10% clinical-meaningfulness threshold is usually about 0.02-0.04 dependency units for the main outcomes, although the accepted core effects are much larger. H131 is due for response. It tested PTEN loss versus no PTEN loss as a predictor of weaker KRAS dependency among KRAS-mutant lines, with direction +1. Discovery R115 was +0.0639 [0.0196, 0.1082], above the approximate clinical scale and nominally positive, but independent validation R119 was -0.0305 [-0.1055, 0.0445], opposite in direction and near null. The validation interval is wide and does not prove absence, but it does not corroborate the discovery and instead leaves clinically meaningful nullity or opposite-direction effects plausible. I therefore reject and close H131. The evidence does not support a consistent PTEN-loss-associated weakening of KRAS dependency in KRAS-mutant lines within this dataset. H149 is newly validated. It tested PTEN loss versus no PTEN loss as a predictor of stronger STAT3 dependency within the CRISPR-KY library, with direction -1. Discovery R137 was +0.1585 [0.0635, 0.2535]. Independent validation R145 was larger and precise at +0.3166 [0.1735, 0.4597], with the lower bound above zero even under stringent validation multiplicity. The two estimates overlap, and the validation removes the prior concern of library-specific attenuation. I accept and close H149. This strengthens the broader PTEN-loss - STAT3 dependency association and supports its robustness across CRISPR libraries. I also reassessed two important claims that already had independent validation but remained unresolved: H3, EGFR amplification versus EGFR dependency, was +0.0252 [-0.0003, 0.0507] in discovery and only +0.0015 [-0.0431, 0.0461] at validation, near null; I reject H3. H39, RB1 loss versus POLR2A dependency, was +0.0249 [-0.0009, 0.0507] in discovery and +0.0002 [-0.0384, 0.0388] at validation, also near null; I reject H39. The supported core findings remain four dataset-specific associations: SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, validated around +0.78 to +0.80; MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency, validated around +0.79 to +0.81; KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, validated around +0.79 in the registered weaker-dependency direction; and PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, validated around +0.27 overall and +0.32 in the KY library after validation. These four effects are large, precisely estimated, and robust across many pre-specified contexts, including batches, culture subsets, mutation contexts, KRAS strata, TP53 strata, ARID1A strata, mutation-burden-high lines, lower-quality screens, and multiple CRISPR-library subsets. The negative evidence is also informative. EGFR amplification is not supported as a meaningful predictor of EGFR dependency after validation. ERBB2 amplification, KRAS mutation, BRAF V600E, TP53 loss effects on MDM2 or RPL11, MYC amplification across several outcomes, RB1 loss effects on POLR2A or KIF18A, STK11 loss, SMAD4 loss, PIK3CA mutation as a direct predictor, NF1 loss, BRCA2 loss, CDKN2A loss independent of SMARCA4 loss, and ARID1A loss alone remain unsupported or unresolved with low information. Constructed research markers D, E, and F behaved as negative controls. Context interaction hunting is now closed: H112 adherent-culture amplification of MSI-high WRN and H135 SLFN11-high amplification of MSI-high WRN were not corroborated by independent validation; H142 and H143 showed no meaningful extension of KEAP1 loss to STAT3 or WRN dependency; H155 did not support MSI-high extension to USP7; H131 showed no supported PTEN-KRAS bypass; and many measured biological, assay, and culture modifiers did not alter the core effects in a validated way. Remaining uncertainty is mostly imprecision or low-priority follow-up rather than contradiction. Several deferred EGFR, ERBB2, TP53, MYC, USP7, and context hypotheses have intervals wide enough to include both clinically meaningful positive and negative values, so they should be described as unsupported rather than definitively null. The most informative next internal analyses are the newly registered high-screen-quality strata, screen_roc_auc >= 0.96, for the four core associations, because they complement the accepted low-quality screen strata and help ensure that the large associations are not artifacts of screen-quality heterogeneity. Beyond that, further exploratory interaction discovery should stop unless hypotheses are externally motivated and pre-specified. The highest-value next evidence would be external replication and adjusted multivariable modeling controlling CRISPR library, screen batch, culture type, screen quality, ploidy, mutation burden, lineage subtype, and other measured covariates.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after iteration 11 synthesis. Core accepted dataset-specific associations: SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H6 R6 +0.784, validation R53 +0.804); MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency (H7 R7 +0.790, validation R40 +0.812); KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H13/R8/R66 around +0.79 in direction +1); PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency (H41 R25 +0.267, validation R26 +0.268). Robustness accepted: batch_a for SMARCA2/WRN/NFE2L2/STAT3, adherent-culture WRN/STAT3 contexts, low screen_roc_auc strata H151-H154, KY SMARCA2 H147, KY NFE2L2 H148, KY STAT3 H149 now validated by H145 and closed; PIK3CA-mutant STAT3 context H70 accepted and validated. New negatives or unresolved-closure: H131 PTEN loss weaker KRAS dependency among KRAS-mutant lines rejected because discovery R115 +0.064 [0.020,0.108] was not corroborated and validation R119 -0.030 [-0.106,0.045] was opposite/near null; H3 EGFR amplification EGFR dependency rejected after validation R13 near null; H39 RB1 loss POLR2A rejected after validation R39 near null; H142/H143/H155 specificity probes negative; H112/H135 interaction probes negative. No previously active claim remains after closing H149. Newly proposed confirmatory high screen_roc_auc >= 0.96 main effects for the four core associations are pending: SMARCA4-SMARCA2, MSI-high-WRN, KEAP1-NFE2L2, and PTEN-STAT3. Future priorities: external replication of the four core associations, adjusted models controlling library, batch, screen quality, culture, ploidy, mutation burden, and subtype, and pre-specified robustness strata; no more exploratory interaction discovery unless externally motivated. Rejected wide intervals should be described as unsupported or non-corroborating, not proof of null."
