ntific gain.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 13 synthesis update: H149 accepted and closed after validation R145. Discovery R137 was positive but only partially above the 0.10 benchmark; validation R145 was larger with lower bound 0.174, supporting clinically meaningful PTEN-loss association with stronger STAT3 dependency in KY-library lines. Four core dataset-specific associations remain supported: SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency; KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency; PTEN loss with much stronger STAT3 dependency. These are robust internally across QC, screen quality, libraries, batch, culture, lineage, mutation burden, aneuploidy, and co-occurring alterations, and independently validated in the main claims. Negative/unsupported: EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, most direct mutation-amplification hypotheses, MYC/RB1/BRCA2/STK11/SMAD4/NF1/ARID1A/CDKN2A as independent predictors, research markers D/E/F, and most context interactions. Unresolved: low-priority comparisons with intervals including null; not proof of absence. No causality or generalizability established. Validation capacity exhausted; no further internal proposals. Next best step is external replication and adjusted multivariable modeling, followed by mechanistic perturbation studies."
