aw exposed-minus-comparator dependency is more negative, i.e. stronger dependency; for interaction claims, a positive signed direction -1 estimate means the exposed effect is more negative/stronger in the named subgroup than in its complement. For direction +1 NFE2L2/KEAP1 claims, a positive signed estimate means weaker NFE2L2 dependency. For the USP7 proposal, TP53 wild-type is defined as exposed and TP53 loss as comparator, so a positive signed direction -1 estimate means wild-type lines have stronger USP7 dependency. Proposed claims should be accepted only if the signed lower bound remains above approximately 0.10 and is biologically plausible; intervals spanning zero and meaningful modification should remain unresolved, and cells below 20 should be recorded as infeasible rather than interpreted as null. These are internal association and specificity analyses in the supplied dataset, not causal or external-validity claims.",
