nfounding remains plausible because age, sex, EMT, and proliferation subgroup analyses are not adjusted for library, batch, Cas9 activity, screen QC, ploidy/aneuploidy, mutation burden, culture, media, or co-alterations. Multiplicity is substantial, so I have accepted only large or otherwise already corroborated effects and avoided interpreting borderline positive interactions. These conclusions are internal dataset associations, not causal or generalizable therapeutic claims.",
