  "narrative": "No new validation was delivered in this turn, and there were no assessments_due or validation response deadlines. Voluntary validation capacity remains exhausted, so I made no accept/reject changes based on new validation. I closed the last two deferred unresolved interaction claims, H232 and H237, as unresolved/closed because their intervals neither demonstrate nor exclude clinically meaningful modification and no validation capacity remains. The signed reporting convention was used throughout: for direction -1 mean differences, a positive estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group; for direction +1 KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 claims, a positive estimate means a less negative score, i.e. weaker dependency; for interactions, a positive estimate means a larger exposed-minus-comparator contrast in the named subgroup than in its complement. I used the run's approximate 0.10 dependency-score-unit relevance benchmark aligned with the 10 percent decision rule.\n\nSupported findings in this supplied lung-lineage CRISPR dataset are four robust internal biomarker-dependency associations, not causal or externally transportable therapeutic claims. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with markedly stronger SMARCA2 dependency: discovery +0.784, 95% CI +0.765 to +0.803 (R6), and independent validation +0.804, CI +0.775 to +0.833 (R53). Second, MSI-high status is associated with markedly stronger WRN dependency: discovery +0.790, CI +0.760 to +0.819 (R7), and validation +0.812, CI +0.765 to +0.858 (R40). Third, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, i.e. a less negative dependency score: discovery +0.796, CI +0.776 to +0.816 (R13), and validation +0.791, CI +0.763 to +0.820 (R66). The originally registered stronger-dependency direction was rejected. Fourth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency: discovery +0.267, CI +0.215 to +0.319 (R25), and validation +0.268, CI +0.188 to +0.348 (R26). The core effects persist across many internal strata, including lineage subtype, CRISPR library, screen batch, screen quality, matched omics availability, mutation burden, aneuploidy, sex/age subsets, and several co-alteration strata. Some validated subset confirmations are particularly important, including PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency in the KY library (H149 discovery +0.158, CI +0.063 to +0.254; validation +0.317, CI +0.174 to +0.460) and MSI-high WRN dependency among TP53-loss lines (H83 discovery +0.833, CI +0.765 to +0.900; validation +0.760, CI +0.674 to +0.847). These are association findings in this dataset; residual confounding by library, batch, Cas9 activity, screen QC, ploidy, aneuploidy, mutation burden, co-alterations, culture, media, and unmeasured model context remains possible.\n\nThe evidence broadly rejects many simple predictor-outcome hypotheses and most candidate interaction modifiers. Direct matched oncogene dependencies were generally not clinically meaningful: KRAS mutation was not meaningfully associated with dependency_KRAS (R1), BRAF V600E with dependency_BRAF (R2), EGFR amplification with dependency_EGFR (discovery near null and validation null, R3/R13), or ERBB2 amplification with dependency_ERBB2 (R4). TP53 loss was not meaningfully associated with dependency_MDM2 (R5), dependency_RPL11, or dependency_POLR2A in most tested settings. MYC amplification was not meaningfully associated with dependency_USP7, dependency_DHX9, dependency_POLR2A, dependency_KRAS, or dependency_STAT3 where tested. ARID1A loss was not supported as an independent SMARCA2 dependency predictor after validation (H21 R15/R80; H202). RB1 loss was rejected for dependency_POLR2A after validation (H39 R23/R39) and was not meaningful for dependency_KIF18A (R24). BRCA2 loss, STK11 loss, NF1 loss, CDKN2A loss, MTAP loss, SMAD4 loss, APC mutation, PIK3CA mutation, PTEN loss for non-STAT3 outcomes, and the constructed research markers D, E, and F were not supported as clinically meaningful predictors. Many interaction hypotheses were rejected as not clinically meaningful, including subtype, culture, batch, Cas9 activity, media serum, mutation burden, aneuploidy, EMT, hypoxia, interferon-gamma, stemness, MYC expression, AXL expression, SLFN11 expression, copy-number, screen-QC, and cross-core co-alteration modifiers of the four core effects. Notably, H112 culture interaction for MSI-high WRN was positive in discovery but null/negative in validation (R94/R105); H131 PTEN-loss KRAS-mutant dependency_KRAS was positive in discovery but negative in validation (R115/R119); H135 SLFN11-high WRN interaction was discovery borderline and validation null/negative (R122/R132). These negative validation results should be treated as stronger than positive discovery-only signals.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty should not be over-interpreted. H232 and H237 remain unresolved/closed: sex-specific modification of PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency was +0.073, CI -0.031 to +0.177 (R221), and growth-rate modification of PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency was +0.035, CI -0.092 to +0.162 (R226). H222 and H224 remain unresolved/closed because their point estimates are small and intervals include both no meaningful modification and at most borderline modification: MSI-high WRN interaction in TP53-loss lines +0.053, CI -0.022 to +0.127 (R211), and KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 interaction in high-growth-rate lines +0.051, CI +0.001 to +0.101 (R213). H197 remains unresolved due to small non-Avana PTEN-loss STAT3 cells. H199, H205, H206, and H213 are infeasible because required cells have fewer than 20 observations and should be treated as noninformative rather than null. Evidenceless unresolved claims are not evidence of absence. The most informative next analysis is not additional untargeted same-dataset mining, which mainly increases false-positive risk and sparse-cell instability. It should be external replication in independent lung cancer model cohorts with prespecified adjustment for library, batch, screen QC, Cas9 activity, ploidy/aneuploidy, mutation burden, subtype, culture, media, and co-alterations. The highest priority replication targets are SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high status with stronger WRN dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, and PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency. If external replication is unavailable, targeted orthogonal perturbation or pharmacologic/genetic experiments should prioritize these four associations, with secondary attention to whether sex or growth rate modifies PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 18 final synthesis. No new validation or due assessments; validation capacity exhausted. Closed H232 and H237 as unresolved/closed because they are imprecise exploratory interactions and no validation remains. Core accepted associations remain: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H6/R6, validated R53); MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency (H7/R7, validated R40); KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H13/R13, validated R66); PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency (H41/R25, validated R26; H149 KY subset validated R145). Negative findings: direct oncogene mutation/amplification dependencies mostly null or not clinically meaningful; EGFR, ERBB2, KRAS, BRAF, TP53-MDM2, MYC-related, RB1-POLR2A/KIF18A, ARID1A independent of SMARCA4, PTEN non-STAT3, BRCA2, STK11, NF1, CDKN2A, MTAP, APC, PIK3CA, SMAD4, research markers D/E/F unsupported. Many interactions rejected or validated null, including culture, batch, Cas9, mutation burden, EMT, hypoxia, interferon-gamma, stemness, MYC/AXL/SLFN11 expression, copy number, subtype, QC strata. Unresolved/closed imprecise interactions: H222, H224, H232, H237; underpowered: H197; infeasible: H199, H205, H206, H213. No further untargeted same-dataset mining planned. Next best: external replication or orthogonal validation of the four core associations, with adjusted designs; if only this dataset can be used, focused targeted tests for sex/growth-rate modification of PTEN/STAT3 only with strong prespecification and feasibility checks."
